gacy entry has no copy set, which reads as unknown rather than empty and is not inferred. An entry a commit adds relative to each parent carries `copied` naming only snapshot registry files. An entry a commit adds relative to each parent without `copied`, or with `copied` naming a file outside the snapshot's registry files, is refused. A whole ledger refuses an entry that omits `copied` after an entry that carries it. A malformed parent or hand-edited ledger lies outside this commit-bound reading. A copied file does not establish that its rows were judged.\""," rationale = \"Row ids identify only approvals and re-attestations, so they cannot establish every registry an act copied. Recording the copied files at the writer preserves that fact for readers without reconstructing it from mutable state, while legacy history remains readable without a false empty-set claim.\""," test_refs = \"TC-400\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-006\""," phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-967\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3963,"oldLines":5,"newStart":3963,"newLines":5,"lines":[" expected = \"Each entry names the files its act copied; a legacy entry parses unchanged with its copy set unknown; an added entry without copied, or with a foreign path, is refused; and a ledger that omits copied after an entry that carries it is refused.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_baseline_snapshot.py::test_an_approval_act_records_the_registry_it_copied; tests/test_baseline_snapshot.py::test_a_reattesting_act_records_the_registry_it_copied; tests/test_baseline_snapshot.py::test_a_traced_reanchor_naming_no_row_records_its_registry; tests/test_baseline_snapshot.py::test_a_mixed_approves_and_reattests_act_records_both_registries; tests/test_baseline_snapshot.py::test_a_reseed_records_every_registry_it_copied; tests/test_baseline_snapshot.py::test_the_needs_file_is_recorded_by_its_canonical_path; tests/tes